  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:4991",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the regulation of HS27 through multiple pathways, with the drug acting as a target for several molecular entities that ultimately converge on HS27. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin interacts with P2X purinoceptor 1, which is targeted by Mollicellin N, and this interaction leads to the activation of HS27. Similarly, doxorubicin is also linked to COLO-792 and NCI-H1304, both of which are targeted by 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn targets HS27. These findings collectively indicate that doxorubicin exerts its effects on HS27 through a series of molecular intermediates, suggesting a potential mechanism involving purinoceptor activation and subsequent downstream signaling pathways. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between doxorubicin and HS27, though the exact nature of the interactions between doxorubicin and the molecular intermediates remains to be fully elucidated.",
